From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 06:33:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] winemetal: MadeiraCtl ops to register probe roles and publish
 the runtime counter block

Op 4 records the calling thread's role (submission worker, Present caller,
ExecuteCommandLists caller) for the per-thread CPU probe; op 5 publishes the
D3D12 runtime's counter block so the probe can read it.

Madeira-commit: ac535fcd69b2a79940f12014902242833881435e
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-dxmt-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c b/src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c
index f288c3e..44fb5ae 100644
--- a/src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c
+++ b/src/winemetal/unix/winemetal_unix.c
@@ -4966,6 +4966,18 @@ static NTSTATUS _madeira_ctl(void *args) {
     a->ret = 1;
     break;
   }
+  case 4: {   /* ml1128: probe role for the CALLING thread (runs on it); len = role char, ptr = Windows TID */
+    extern void ios_xp_set_role(int role, uint64_t wtid);
+    ios_xp_set_role((int)a->len, a->ptr);
+    a->ret = 1;
+    break;
+  }
+  case 5: {   /* ml1128: the PE counter block the probe samples */
+    extern volatile uint64_t ios_xp_pe_block, ios_xp_pe_len;
+    ios_xp_pe_len = a->len; ios_xp_pe_block = a->ptr;
+    a->ret = 1;
+    break;
+  }
   case 2: {
     char v[512];
     if (madeira_cfg_get(a->name, v, sizeof v)) {
